A Branch target built at run time, missing the LABEL keyword in the
computed text. branch_target_label deliberately checks only single string
literals, so nothing reports the dead jump.
Known issue: #321 (computed Branch() targets never jump - not yet
diagnosed).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE JumpByName;
	:PARAMETERS sStage;
	:DECLARE sTarget, nVisits;
	nVisits := 0;
	sTarget := Upper(sStage);
	:LABEL FINISH;
	nVisits := nVisits + 1;
	:IF nVisits < 2;
		Branch(sTarget);
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN nVisits;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE JumpByName;
	:PARAMETERS sStage;
	:DECLARE sTarget, nVisits;

	nVisits := 0;
	sTarget := Upper(sStage);
	:LABEL FINISH;
	nVisits := nVisits + 1;

	:IF nVisits < 2;
		Branch(sTarget);
	:ENDIF;

	:RETURN nVisits;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
6:2-6:8 warning deprecated_keyword: ':LABEL' is legacy flow control used with Branch(); prefer structured control flow in new code
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
6:2-6:8 warning deprecated_keyword: ':LABEL' is legacy flow control used with Branch(); prefer structured control flow in new code
